<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n90659" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόφαν-τος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>appearing at a distance,
				far seen</i>, hence <i>far-famed</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. σοφίᾳ καθ᾽ Ἕλλανας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					1.117
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>foreshown</i>, esp. by an oracle, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμοὶ γὰρ ἦν π. ἐκ πατρός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					1159
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς τὸ θεῖον ἦν π</span>. as
			the divine <i>oracle</i> ran, ib.<i><span class="en">
				1163
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥς σφι αἰεὶ τὠυτὸ π. ἐγίνετο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					5.63
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόφαντα δέ σφι . . ἐγίνετο</span>
			<i>oracles</i> were delivered to them, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				9.93
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σημεῖον π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				18.6.9
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
